      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242742",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/d6/d6b6c5c7c79189fa446c1ef25cc3c93a2c76bbb27e096083a268fc83c20e118f.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $X_{1}$ and $Z_{1}$ are the midpoints of $YZ^(\u2015)$ and $XY^(\u2015)$, respectively. You may assume without proof that\n$\\frac{YZ_{1}}{YX} = \\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nNow, consider the following statement:\n\n> $\\frac{X_{1}Z_{1}}{XZ} = \\frac{1}{2}$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of this statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $X_{1}$ is the midpoint of $YZ^(\u2015)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 2 | $YX_{1} = \\frac{1}{2}YZ$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $\\frac{YX_{1}}{YZ} = \\frac{1}{2}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $\\frac{YZ_{1}}{YX} = \\frac{1}{2}$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 5 | $\\frac{YZ_{1}}{YX} = \\frac{YX_{1}}{YZ}$ | {{field-5}} |\n| 6 | $\u2220XYZ\u2245\u2220Z_{1}YX_{1}$ | {{field-6}} |\n| 7 | $\u25b3XYZ\u223c\u25b3Z_{1}YX_{1}$ | {{field-7}} |\n| 8 | $\\frac{X_{1}Z_{1}}{XZ} = \\frac{YX_{1}}{YZ}$ | {{field-8}} |\n| 9 | $\\frac{X_{1}Z_{1}}{XZ} = \\frac{1}{2}$ | {{field-9}} |"
    },
