      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242790",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/80/8045fa1d3e485bd5c271609e9cf46e0dfde428fcc84b04cdde400322f7cfa683.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $U$ and $V$ are the midpoints of $YZ^(\u2015)$ and $XZ^(\u2015)$, respectively. You may assume without proof that\n\n$\\frac{ZV}{ZX} = \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{ZU}{ZY} = \\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nNow, consider the following statement:\n\n> $UV^(\u2015)\u2225XY^(\u2015)$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\u2220XZY\u2245\u2220VZU$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 2 | $\\frac{ZV}{ZX} = \\frac{1}{2}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $\\frac{ZU}{ZY} = \\frac{1}{2}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $\\frac{ZV}{ZX} = \\frac{ZU}{ZY}$, | {{field-4}} |\n| 5 | $\u25b3XZY\u223c\u25b3VZU$ | {{field-5}} |\n| 6 | $\u2220ZVU\u2245\u2220X$ | {{field-6}} |\n| 7 | $UV^(\u2015)\u2225XY^(\u2015)$ | {{field-7}} |"
    }
  ],
